WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:08.383
This is Anthropic, Read Aloud. Today: Open call for guest investigators in the life sciences.

2
00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:13.032
Open call for guest investigators in the life sciences.

3
00:00:13.482 --> 00:00:18.193
From Anthropic Newsroom, published October 22, 2026.

4
00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:25.571
Today, we’re inviting members of the life sciences community to apply to work with us on special projects.

5
00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:46.427
We’re looking for proposals from principal investigators and their research groups at academic institutions, nonprofits, or government labs who want to use Claude to investigate key questions in causal human biology, structural and computational molecular biology, medicinal chemistry, drug discovery, and clinical science.

6
00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:49.329
You can submit a proposal for a project here.

7
00:00:49.779 --> 00:01:06.526
Over 8 to 12 weeks, guest investigators will work directly with Anthropic researchers on a problem of interest and produce the analyses, artifacts, and tools that will be most helpful for them in their work. Our team will run our models and harnesses at no cost to them.

8
00:01:06.976 --> 00:01:23.693
We’ll work together to publish these outputs and open-source the accompanying data and code. Guest investigators retain the rights to their data at every step during their project. They will also have the rights to any independent follow-on research that might come out of our collaboration.

9
00:01:24.143 --> 00:01:46.270
We’re looking for applicants who can clearly explain how they would benefit from direct collaboration with Anthropic’s researchers. Applicants should also make a reasonable case that their outputs (for example, preliminary discoveries, answers to open questions, open-source datasets, or public resources) can be produced within the 8- to 12-week collaboration period.

10
00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:52.086
There may be an option for extension beyond the initial collaboration period for some projects.

11
00:01:52.536 --> 00:02:04.916
We understand that the results for most open problems of interest will take much longer to validate, but we’re looking for proposals that can produce some preliminary evidence in a relatively short amount of time.

12
00:02:05.366 --> 00:02:18.698
We aren’t asking for guest investigators to give us their data, either in the application or during the collaboration, and we’re requesting that applicants include only publicly available information in their application materials.

13
00:02:19.148 --> 00:02:37.896
Applications will be open for approximately 14 days, and we’ll strive to notify selected participants by email approximately 14 days after applications close. We look forward to potentially expanding this effort in the future as we learn more about how we can best support the scientific community.

14
00:02:38.346 --> 00:02:57.892
This program is one of several initiatives Anthropic is pursuing to invest more heavily in the life sciences and the broader scientific research community. Scientists who would like direct access to our most capable publicly available models for biology can apply to join our Life Sciences Verification Program.

15
00:02:58.012 --> 00:03:09.935
We’ve also continued to support researchers through our A I for Science initiative, which provides scientists with Claude credits to accelerate their progress toward making scientific discoveries.

16
00:03:10.935 --> 00:03:29.098
That was Open call for guest investigators in the life sciences, from Anthropic Newsroom, published October 22, 2026. Read the original at anthropic dot com. This unofficial audio edition was generated automatically for the podcast Anthropic, Read Aloud.
